@spec arrange_tidy_modal_spec  src=tests/specs/arrange_tidy_modal_spec.lua  loc=130  cases=3
@exercises configManager (h.cm), arrangeView (av)
@surface   cm:set, av:seedTidy
@harness   mk, reaper:setTrackName, reaper:addItem, reaper:setProjectTracks

# Intent
  The tidy editor's base list, drawn over a fake imgui: does the Add button see what stands
  in the new-base field? ReaImGui hands a buffer back only on a frame its InputText returns
  true, so a field flagged EnterReturnsTrue reads blank to every gesture but Enter.

# Helpers
  @fn mkTidyModal(harness)  @ 62-89
      -- Build the tidy modal's body over a real av, and return it with the state openTidyModal seeds.
  @fn drawWith(harness, text, gesture)  @ 92-97
      -- One frame of the modal, with the field holding `text` and `gesture` committing it.
  @fn holds(bases, name)  @ 99-102

# Cases
  @case 'the Add button appends the base standing in the field'  [harness]  @ 106-111
  @case 'Enter in the field appends it too'  [harness]  @ 115-120
  @case 'an untouched field adds nothing'  [harness]  @ 124-128

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call cm:set  @ 64
  @use call av:seedTidy  @ 86

